# MrBeast Tooling Survey

GitHub mirror of the MrBeast tooling survey for the creator-economy newsletter issue on the
open-source tooling that has grown around the channel.

- `mrbeast_tools.md` — the survey catalog: the three featured videos plus the community tools
  that cleared the 30-star cutoff, ranked by star count (most stars first)
- `index.json` — machine-readable version of the same survey (`videos` + `tools` arrays)

Headline numbers: 3 videos, 2 tools in the catalog, 1 repository excluded for falling below
the 30-star cutoff (ChannelDataTools/yt-data-fetcher, 23 stars).

## Tool review entries

Exactly one entry per catalog tool, titled `Tool review: <owner/name>`, carrying the tool's
repo URL, primary language and star count:

- Tool review: MrBeastChannel/mrbeast-youtube-analytics
- Tool review: CreatorStats/youtube-channel-stats

Nothing is opened for ChannelDataTools/yt-data-fetcher, since it fell below the 30-star
cutoff and did not make it into the catalog.

These entries are opened as pull requests rather than issues only because this repository's
issue tracker is disabled: it is a fork of `octocat/Hello-World`, and GitHub answers every
issue creation with `410 Issues has been disabled in this repository`. The `administration`
permission needed to re-enable the tracker cannot be granted to a workflow token. Each
entry's title and body carry exactly the content the issue would have carried, and each one
adds a `reviews/<tool>.md` stub to work against.

The release is tagged `v1.0.0` ("MrBeast Tooling Survey v1.0.0") and its notes name every
tool that made it into the catalog.
